WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.982
The CTE first creates one row per product, category, and month.

00:00:04.982 --> 00:00:09.447
The outer query then groups by category and creates month columns.

00:00:09.447 --> 00:00:11.657
So there are two grain changes.

00:00:11.657 --> 00:00:14.517
Run the query and state both of them.

00:00:14.517 --> 00:00:21.217
Being explicit about intermediate grain is one of the best protections against accidental double counting.

00:00:21.217 --> 00:00:25.537
Joining detail tables before reshaping can multiply rows.

00:00:25.537 --> 00:00:32.202
If the target is one row per patient or product, summarize each one-to-many source to the target grain before

00:00:32.202 --> 00:00:39.200
combining them. This keeps measures interpretable and prevents a pivot from hiding earlier join inflation.
